# Patterns to ignore when building packages.
# Matched against the chart directory, one pattern per line.

# --- the two that actually matter here -------------------------------------
#
# tests/ holds helm-unittest specs and ci/ holds the value sets chart-testing
# installs. Both are development inputs: they are read from the working tree, never
# from the packaged artifact, and shipping them would put megabytes of test fixtures
# into every `helm pull`.
#
# The leading slash is load-bearing. .helmignore matches like .gitignore: a pattern
# with no leading slash matches a directory of that name at ANY depth, so a bare
# `tests/` silently swallows templates/tests/ as well — and templates/tests/ is the
# `helm test` hook, which very much needs to ship. The symptom is
# "TEST SUITE: None" from a release that plainly has a test, and nothing anywhere
# says why. Anchored to the chart root, it excludes only what it should.
/tests/
/ci/

# --- the usual noise --------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
.git/
.gitignore
.idea/
.vscode/
*.tmproj
*.swp
*.bak
*.tgz
*.orig
*~
